WEBVTT

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:04.020
This is the Sakuragi Institute
in Kuchiba City.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:04.980
Ring, ring, ring!

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.330
It’s your scheduled wake-up time!

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.470
Ring, ring, ring!

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.210
It’s your scheduled wake-up—

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.450
Satoshi… It’s morning…

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.580
Ring, ring, ring…

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.460
Go, Satoshi! Wake up!

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.890
Did you forget what day it is?

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:32.790
Thank you all for coming to
the Pokémon Orienteering event!

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.640
I’m Sakuragi,
the director of this institute.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.580
I’m Kikuna, an assistant.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.210
I’m Renji, also an assistant.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:44.440
And your guides today will be
these two special people!

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.400
Oh… I’m Satoshi!

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.180
I-I’m Go.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.280
Nice to meet you.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.240
Hey, Go!

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.950
Oh, Sota!

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.700
Quiet down…

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.700
So, does everyone know
what we’ll be researching today?

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.200
<i>Pokémon!</i>

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.770
Correct! Pocket Monsters,
or Pokémon for short!

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:07.670
The strange, strange creatures
that live on this planet!

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.230
All kinds of Pokémon live
in all kinds of places in this city.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:16.480
I want you to learn new things
about these Pokémon,

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.970
and grow to love them more!

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.400
That’s what made me come up
with this Pokémon Orienteering day!

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.990
We had you split
into three teams, correct?

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:29.850
Look over here.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:34.280
All three teams will soon set off
for their goal: Kuchiba Port.

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:40.480
And you’ll be competing to see which team
finds the most Pokémon before reaching the goal.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.330
Try to find as many Pokémon as possible!

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:45.830
Yes!

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.950
All right, let’s get started!

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:49.960
The Pokémon Orienteering…

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.090
Let’s go!

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:58.840
PocketMonsters

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.260
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.840
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.560
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.430
And skip the slow send-off

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.770
Be it through fire or through water

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:14.440
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:18.940
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:24.200
Each and every one of my memories

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.790
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.710
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:38.460
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:45.470
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:49.680
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.020
Let's have a fight!

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.730
1: Once the battle's done

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.560
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:59.900
On 3, let's be friends!

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:06.570
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:11.910
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:14.410
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:18.540
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.340
I choose you!

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:29.350
Satoshi and Go!!
Go Towards Your Dreams!

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.850
This is where we split up into three routes.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.610
Later, Director Sakuragi!

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:35.350
See you at the goal!

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:37.090
Yes. Be careful!

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:46.330
Look at that!
Do you know what Pokémon it is?

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.220
The answer is…

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:55.330
Persian. Siamese Cat Pokémon.
Normal type.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.110
A Persian’s six bold whiskers…

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:59.720
…sense air movements to determine
what is in its vicinity.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.930
Oh, Nyarth!

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:11.050
Nyarth. Monster Cat Pokémon.
Normal type.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:14.440
When it sees a shiny object,
the gold coin on its head shines too.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.720
Look at that! Persian is using its whiskers.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.310
Right, let’s follow them!

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:31.910
Can we really?

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.110
Look.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:50.970
Koratta. Mouse Pokémon.
Normal type.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:53.340
It will make its nest anywhere.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:56.520
A battle might start.

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.040
Here comes help!

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:12.010
Ratta.
Koratta’s evolved form.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:16.210
Gnaws on anything with its tough fangs.
It can even topple concrete buildings by gnawing on them.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:22.040
That’s Fury Swipes!

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:24.470
Desperate Tackle!

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:26.520
Fangs of Rage!

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.210
Power Gem!

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.520
Guardie, Roar!

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:37.620
Watching them this close
is too dangerous.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.310
Miss Junsa!

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.570
No, I just wanted to show everyone
from the Pokémon Orienteering what battling is like…

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:44.240
“Everyone”?

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.500
Yeah! These guys…

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:49.170
Huh? Huh?! Why?

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:52.490
You shouldn’t leave small children
unattended like that!

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.380
Got it…

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:00.340
Hey! You should try touching Guardie!

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.960
Yay!

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.510
Good dog!
So fluffy!

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.580
So cute!

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:11.560
Pokémon Orienteering?

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:14.810
It says they’re headed for Kuchiba Port.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.050
This is a chance to get the brat boy’s Pikachu…

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:21.320
…<i>and</i> loads of other Pokémon, too!

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:24.000
I got a great plan, meow!

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.660
Over there?

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.320
Or over here?

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:36.250
Look! If that's this big building on the map,
that means we’re going this way!

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.250
Yeah!

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.380
This kinda reminds me
of Professor Okido’s Pokémon camp.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.980
Those innocent childhood days
sure were great!

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:50.330
But you’re <i>still</i> a kid, though?

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:54.810
I’m a Pokémon Trainer!
There are no “kids” or “adults” among trainers!

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:59.350
Satoshi will gladly battle
any grown-up opponents!

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:02.940
I thought you weren’t interested
in Pokémon battling?

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.820
It’s just that I don’t fight
<i>pointless</i> battles.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.170
I’ll battle if I have to
in order to catch Pokémon, yeah?

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.050
Oh, is that so?

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:14.450
A Pokémon!

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:16.700
It’s a Poppo!

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:19.400
Watch me! I’ll catch it!

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.270
Go, Monster Ball!

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:22.360
Great!

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:29.090
All right!

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:35.850
Poppo’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:37.610
Okay!

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:39.360
There’s something over there, too!

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:40.730
I got this.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.730
Monster Ball, go, go!

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.610
Okay!

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:53.240
Nidoran’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.410
It’s a double catch!
Both a male <i>and</i> a female Nidoran!

00:07:56.410 --> 00:08:01.090
Come on… You have to teach them
about the Pokémon before you catch them.

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:03.250
Don’t worry! I’ll do that now!

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:10.640
Poppo! Tiny Bird Pokémon!
Normal/Flying type!

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:15.890
It is docile and prefers to avoid conflict!
If disturbed, however, it can ferociously strike back!

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.590
Nidoran! Poison Pin Pokémon!
Poison type!

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:23.480
The male evolves into
Nidorino and then Nidoking!

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:29.150
The smaller, more docile female
evolves into Nidorina and then Nidoqueen!

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:33.910
There, there…
I’m so glad you’re my partners now!

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:36.200
Another Pokémon spotted!

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.780
What? Where?! Where?!

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.440
There’s something over there, too!

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:41.290
What?!

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:42.660
That’s a Nyoromo!

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:43.790
Go!

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.170
Nazonokusa’s data will be added—

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:54.180
Nyoromo’s data will be added—

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.440
All right!

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:58.950
You’re as innocent and excitable
as you’ve ever been…

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:06.920
They like you.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.200
You’re so lucky, Big Sis!

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:09.160
Let go of me!
You’re so lucky, Big Sis!

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:10.190
Let go of me!

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.400
It’s a Kamonegi! You’re mine!

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.580
Geez!

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.050
I can see the port!

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:27.000
Amazing!

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.650
Pidgeon and Pidgeot!

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:35.670
Pidgeon. Bird Pokémon.
Normal/Flying type.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:40.390
Very protective of its sprawling territorial area,
this Pokémon will fiercely peck at any intruder.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:43.410
Pidgeot. Pidgeon’s evolved form…

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:48.210
This is an official
battle announcement.

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:49.690
That means…

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.910
What’s an “official battle”?

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:59.390
It is a battle between two trainers
registered in the Pokémon World Championships,

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:03.310
fought so that they may increase their ranking.

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:07.770
Would you like to battle? Or not?

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:11.300
Of course I’ll battle! Or, so I’d <i>like</i> to say, but…

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.840
We want to see a Pokémon battle!

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.720
Really?
All right, then I’ll do it!

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.040
Official battle appointment made!

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.900
Welcome! Welcome!

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:27.480
The Pokémon World Championships
has approved this Normal Class battle!

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:30.250
I’m Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:33.360
I’m Seiya, from Kogane City
in the Johto Region!

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:38.130
This battle will be a 1v1.

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:41.620
Now, allow me to explain
the official rules!

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:46.940
Whichever trainer incapacitates
the opponent’s Pokémon wins!

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:50.740
I shall be the judge of this battle.

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:54.010
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:55.170
3!

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:56.340
2!

00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:57.510
1!

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:58.760
Go!

00:10:58.760 --> 00:10:59.960
Here we go!

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:02.300
Pikachu! I choose you!

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:12.330
Meganium. Herb Pokémon.
Grass type.

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:14.680
Chicorita’s final evolution.

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:19.530
The aroma that rises from its petals contains a substance
that calms aggressive feelings.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:24.530
Sorry to say, but Electric-type moves
won’t be very effective against the Grass-type Meganium!

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:27.060
I know! But I won’t lose!

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:31.500
Battle start!

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.310
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:43.510
Flying
. Normal .
Kamonegi

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:46.360
Victory goes to he who strikes first!
Use Razor Leaf!

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:49.810
Electroweb!

00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:56.230
Body Slam!

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:58.440
Dodge!

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:01.570
Continue using Body Slam!

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.070
Dodge and use Iron Tail!

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:10.080
Razor Leaf!

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:13.380
Hang in there, Pikachu!

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:14.880
100,000 Volts!

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.640
Stay strong! Solar Beam!

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:26.650
Let’s finish this before
the Solar Beam fires!

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:28.060
Lightning Speed!

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:37.730
All right…
Let the power of the light explode!

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:51.370
Nobody’s ever managed to stay standing
after taking Soshinium’s Solar Beam.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.040
It’s over.

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:55.820
Pikachu!

00:12:56.520 --> 00:12:57.640
Are you okay?!

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:00.960
What? You’re kidding!

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:02.430
B-Body Slam!

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:09.930
Use Meganium’s momentum against it!
Iron Tail!

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:23.700
Meganium is unable to battle!
Pikachu wins!

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:26.660
As such, the winner is
Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.130
We did it!

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.650
Based on the results of this battle,

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:36.060
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:39.880
Nice work.

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:42.250
Take a good, long rest.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:44.010
Seiya.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:47.630
That was a great battle, Satoshi!

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:48.800
Thank you!

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:50.850
I won’t lose next time!

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.180
Likewise!

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:03.210
That was such a cool
Pokémon battle, Mister!

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:06.190
Thanks! But being “cool”
isn’t everything.

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:11.250
I believe that battling helps you
know Pokémon better,

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.570
and grow closer to them.

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:16.460
That’s why I battle.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:22.590
Latest rankings.

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:26.510
1,512th place…

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:29.210
We went way up!

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:32.810
1,512th place in what?

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:40.690
It means that I’m the 1,512th strongest trainer
registered in the Pokémon World Championships!

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:42.820
Is that strong?

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:45.710
Maybe not…

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:48.350
There’s over 10,000
registered trainers,

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:50.950
so I guess I still have
a long way to go!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.620
Who’s the strongest?

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.870
Mr. Dande from the Galar Region!

00:14:55.510 --> 00:15:00.540
I’m participating in the Championships
so that I can to battle him!

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:03.550
So you’re gonna become
the strongest, too?

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:08.740
Yeah! And then I’ll have gotten one step closer
to my dream of being a Pokémon Master!

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.000
Go!

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:17.020
Betobeta’s data will be added—

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:20.350
Go!

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:24.270
Abo’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:26.900
Amazing!
You’re on a catching spree!

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:31.410
Yeah! I believe that this helps you
know Pokémon better,

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:34.230
and come to a deeper
understanding with them.

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:36.410
That’s why I catch.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.950
Wanna see the Pokémon
I’ve collected?

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.210
Yeah!

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:45.530
There’s so many!

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:52.180
It’s just 37 for now,
but my dream is to catch <i>every</i> Pokémon!

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.940
Every Pokémon?

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:55.500
Yeah!

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:58.110
And then I’ll reach Mew!

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:03.190
That future lies in my hands!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:05.020
So cool!

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:07.940
There you go,
talking big again…

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:10.280
Back again?!

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.110
If a curve ball didn’t work,
I’ll try a fastball!

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:19.040
Are you okay?

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:22.440
Yellow Team has
reached the port.

00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:24.170
What about the other teams?

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:27.000
Blue Team is coming from the east.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.670
And Red Team is approaching
Kuchiba Port from the west.

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:32.180
Got it.

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:34.640
We found plenty of Pokémon!

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:37.070
I hope our team wins!

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:39.430
Hey!

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:42.310
Director Sakuragi!

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:44.270
Dad!

00:16:45.590 --> 00:16:47.460
Everyone arrived at
more or less the same time.

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:49.030
Big news!

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:52.110
Lugia’s appeared!

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:54.410
Lugia?!

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:55.530
Where is it?!

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:58.720
Well, look over there!

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:00.440
Awesome!

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:01.960
All right! I’ll catch it!

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:03.670
Hold on!

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:05.940
That’s a Legendary Pokémon!

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:07.540
We’d better fight a Raid Battle!

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:10.440
Okay! Let’s go, Pikachu!

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.380
Right, let’s do this, Rabbifoot!

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:15.400
Huh?

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:20.310
Big Sis, it looks like
Wanpachi’s fired up, too!

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:21.310
Huh?!

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:26.650
Hold it!

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.400
Stay right there!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:29.480
Eh?

00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:31.060
Huh?!

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:31.900
What?!

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:37.370
If you ask us “Eh? Huh?! What?!”,

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:41.120
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:44.440
To protect the world from devastation.

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:46.930
To preserve world peace.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:50.920
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.510
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:54.940
Musashi!

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:55.970
Kojiro!

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:59.430
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:02.810
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:05.640
Just kidding, meow!

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:11.860
Team Rocket! You again?!

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:13.200
Then is that Lugia…

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.700
It’s a fake made from balloons!

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:18.950
Wanpachi!

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:19.970
Wait!

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:21.870
Give us our Pokémon back!

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.280
Not a chance!

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:26.120
Byenara, meow!

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:35.510
Lugia?!

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:37.510
No way!

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.310
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:51.330
Well, in that case…

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:53.340
Vending, come on!

00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:05.360
Rocket…

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:06.840
Vending…

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:08.160
Secret!

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.670
Straight from Team Rocket HQ!

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.670
Face our cool Pokémon!

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:18.510
The Armor Bird Pokémon,
Airm’d!

00:19:20.020 --> 00:19:22.010
The Bat Pokémon, Crobat!

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:24.020
Go! Let’s do a tag battle!

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:24.680
Yeah!

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:26.640
Let’s go, Rabbifoot!

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:28.960
Pikachu!

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:31.830
Air Cutter!

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:34.400
Dodge and use 100,000 Volts!
Dodge and use Ember!

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:35.020
Dodge and use 100,000 Volts!

00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:40.950
We can’t reach them!

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:42.080
Air Slash!

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:45.120
Dodge!

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:51.020
Go! Have Rabbifoot fire
an Ember at Pikachu!

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:52.800
A combo attack, huh?

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:56.670
All right! Rabbifoot!
Aim an Ember at Pikachu!

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:59.050
Send it away with Iron Tail!

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:09.630
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:15.930
We did it!

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:17.150
Yeah!

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:26.350
All right, let me
announce the results.

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:29.610
The ones who found
the most Pokémon were…

00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:31.000
Yellow Team!

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.170
All right!

00:20:32.170 --> 00:20:33.820
We lost…

00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:35.670
But it was super fun!

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:39.170
Yeah! It made me want to
learn more about Pokémon!

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:41.490
I’m glad to hear it.

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:42.180
Me, too.

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:46.430
And I want to catch every Pokémon, too,
just like you, Mister Go!

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:50.600
I wanna get as good at Pokémon battling
as Mister Satoshi!

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:54.030
I see. Well, you’d better
hurry and turn ten…

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.900
…so you can make
your trainer débuts!

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:57.100
Yeah!

00:20:57.100 --> 00:21:00.610
Looks like the Pokémon Orienteering
was a huge hit!

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:03.860
Dream big and
don’t give up, everyone!

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:05.680
Yeah!

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.590
Go?

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:12.540
All right! Time to end this!

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:16.900
Psyche!

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:17.840
Nice!

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:26.410
I got the cheeky Kamonegi!

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:32.690
When all’s said and done, Satoshi and Go
will keep going towards their respective dreams!

00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:35.810
Dream big and
don’t give up, everyone!

